      "url": "https://cseweb.ucsd.edu/~kube/cls/100/Lectures/lec12/lec12-19.html",
      "note": "Read 2026-11-17 through a summarizing fetch. Distance is 'the number of edges on the shortest path'; BFS visits the start, then its neighbors, then theirs, and 'as soon as we visit a node in the graph, we know the shortest path from s to it'. That depth-first search returns the first path it reaches, not the shortest, is the author's statement."
    },
    {
      "cite": "Author's scenario (REQ-333)",
