  "brief": {
    "situation": "You maintain planner.py at Harbor County Transit (fictional). It models routes as an unweighted graph (an edge is one bus ride between transfer points) and should return the trip with the fewest rides. Riders get long, valid trips when short ones exist. The planner launches at 18:00. It is 17:05.",
    "handover": [
      "The graph has 3,400 transfer points and 11,200 edges, stored as adjacency lists.",
      "The search returns the first path it reaches the destination by."
    ],
    "howItWorks": [
      "Pick a step from the action list: look, change, check or ship. Nothing you pick is typed or executed: every step shows an authored result.",
      "Each step takes working minutes, and the clock moves by the minutes it takes. The deadline runs on the same clock.",
      "Shipping is final for this case. Afterwards you record what you found and explain your reasoning."
    ]
  },
