    "modelReasoning": "Valid trips with too many rides mean the search finds a path, not the shortest. It is depth-first: it follows one branch to the end and returns the first path that reaches the goal. In an unweighted graph, breadth-first search visits stops in order of distance, so the first time it reaches the goal is by a fewest-edge path, in O(V + E). Dijkstra with weight 1 is correct but adds a log factor; enumerating all paths is exponential."
